{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pulls/702","id":4732739493,"node_id":"PR_kwDORnQJEs8AAAABGhffpQ","html_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pull/702","diff_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pull/702.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pull/702.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/issues/702","number":702,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"test(checkout): #661 round 7 boundary tests","user":{"login":"BradleyGleavePortfolio","id":264851314,"node_id":"U_kgDOD8lPcg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264851314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio","html_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> **Status (2026-10-04, round 7).** Tests-only PR stacked on #661 (base `agent/clinic/b-secrets-3`). It carries the regression tests for the #661 round 7 fix of Sol B-661-3 (list boundary, comment 5977638148 at `c7ee15f0`), kept out of #661 under the operator's no-net-growth ruling (SIZE ASSESSMENT, comment 5977489245). Lands with #661 as one unit (guide rule 11); never retarget it to main on its own. Needs both lenses at its exact head. Do not merge without audit.\n\n**Tier:** T4.\n**Why:** Money and entitlement: the tests prove that a paid one-time purchase whose payment failed and then succeeded gets its access back however many never-activated purchases share its PaymentIntent. Tests only; no source, schema, workflow or dependency change.\n**T4 trigger scan:** payments/Stripe data path: tests only (real `CheckoutWebhookHandlerService`, `CheckoutService`, `PurchaseFanoutService` and Prisma on real PostgreSQL; Stripe is a test double). Auth/tenancy: NO. Schema/migration: NO. New env name: NO. Workflow, `scripts/ci/*`, branch protection: NO (the spec is already in the `mwb-3-live-tests` list). Logging/redaction: NO.\n**T3 trigger scan:** none (no contract or shared primitive changes).\n**Bounded T1:** none.\n**Canonical builder:** agent 117 (B-661-R7-117).\n**Parent owner:** #661 (`agent/clinic/b-secrets-3`), fix round 7 at `c76491692fd03b7304416cf68c7589098f9817ea`.\n**Acceptance evidence:** One file, `test/checkout-settlement.live.spec.ts` (+231 / -4), runs in `mwb-3-live-tests` on real PostgreSQL with the full Prisma schema. New block `B-661-3 round 7: the owner query is complete at any number of adopted purchases`, `it.each([9, 10, 12])`: a hosted purchase (the owner) is created first; then `count` real native reservations are made through `CheckoutService.createPaymentIntentForClient` with the provider replies held, and each is adopted onto the owner's PaymentIntent by a real `payment_intent.payment_failed` delivery (metadata fallback) in its own held transaction; the owner's real `checkout.session.completed` activates it (one PurchaseFanout row, a deferred split), a real failure revokes it and cancels its drop, then the same PaymentIntent succeeds. Purchase reads that name no order are answered in an adversarial legal order (`legalOrder`: findMany newest first, findFirst oldest first). The test asserts the boundary itself (`count + 1` failed purchases on the PaymentIntent, exactly one activation record, an unfiltered ten-row read misses the owner from ten on), then: result `{ claimed: true, purchase_id: owner, reason: 'payment_recovered' }` (no second split descriptor), owner `paid` / entitled / `last_error` null, its drop pending again, every adopted purchase still `payment_failed` and unentitled with no activation record, exactly one PurchaseFanout row; after the held native replies land, every adopted purchase holds its own PaymentIntent and stays unentitled, and a redelivered success is `no_matching_purchase` with nothing changed. The existing live tests are unchanged (pool raised from 8 to 16 connections for the held transactions).\nFailing-before (these tests against #661 round 6 `c7ee15f0`, tests commit `617add10`): 2 failed / 31 passed, `tsc --noEmit` green, in [run 37186266591](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37186266591): the 10 and 12 cases return `{ claimed: false, reason: 'checkout_session_activates' }`; the 9 case (control) passes. After (this head's tree, #661 round 7 merged in): 190 / 190 across the live spec and the 11 affected unit suites, `tsc --noEmit` green, in [run 37186426457](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37186426457). The lane-only global setup that starts the runner's PostgreSQL is not in this PR.\n**Promotion triggers:** re-audit if `activatedFailedPurchases` stops filtering activation, one-time and subscription in the query, or if a PurchaseFanout row can be deleted while its purchase exists (it is the activation record).\n\n## What changed\n\n| Finding | Test | Before (c7ee15f0) | After |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B-661-3 (Sol, round 6 verdict 5977638148): the owner lookup capped every failed row of the PaymentIntent at ten before checking activation | `B-661-3 round 7: ... behind %i never-activated purchases ...` (9, 10, 12) | 10 and 12 fail (`checkout_session_activates`), 9 passes | all pass |\n\nSize: 235 changed lines, all test.\n","created_at":"2026-10-04T07:43:28Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T16:47:12Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"6e93fd6d6a89a140316e616048271cc1c883573f","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":11278565662,"node_id":"LA_kwDORnQJEs8AAAACoEFBHg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/labels/size/size/XL","name":"size/size/XL","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pulls/702/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pulls/702/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/issues/702/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/statuses/20d2eb4f696f5e9b4966000f88bd1cdf76ba4ddb","head":{"label":"BradleyGleavePortfolio:agent/clinic/b-661-r7-tests","ref":"agent/clinic/b-661-r7-tests","sha":"20d2eb4f696f5e9b4966000f88bd1cdf76ba4ddb","user":{"login":"BradleyGleavePortfolio","id":264851314,"node_id":"U_kgDOD8lPcg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264851314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio","html_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/gists{/gi